13ie|n|The hard, white, opaque, fine-grained substance constituting the tusks of the elephant. It is a variety of dentine, characterized by the minuteness and close arrangement of the tubes, as also by their double flexure. It is used in manufacturing articles of ornament or utility. ; The tusks themselves of the elephant, etc. ; Any carving executed in ivory. ; Teeth; as, to show one's ivories.	a:ei,41,3~ei,41,3	n:u2w,110,26~u2w,110,26	N:22xw,102,23;dfl,84,2;9rv,74,26~9rv,74,26;22xw,102,23;dfl,84,2
13ie|a|The hard, white, opaque, fine-grained substance constituting the tusks of the elephant. It is a variety of dentine, characterized by the minuteness and close arrangement of the tubes, as also by their double flexure. It is used in manufacturing articles of ornament or utility. ; The tusks themselves of the elephant, etc. ; Any carving executed in ivory. ; Teeth; as, to show one's ivories.	j:dfl,74,1~dfl,74,1
13ig|n|A plant of the genus Hedera (H. helix), common in Europe. Its leaves are evergreen, dark, smooth, shining, and mostly five-pointed; the flowers yellowish and small; the berries black or yellow. The stem clings to walls and trees by rootlike fibers.	a:1mo0,20,4;wz,15,3~1mo0,20,4;wz,15,3	n:1jwd,102,11;8p6,91,6;fti,79,114;ugz,46,7~fti,79,114;1jwd,102,11;ugz,46,7;8p6,91,6	N:15jf,106,41;uk4,73,3;96w,60,30;25l6,25,5~15jf,106,41;96w,60,30;25l6,25,5;uk4,73,3
